    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0132" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg36"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Toivnsend</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 38 of January 27 last
                    and to the Department’s No. 37 of March 8 in reply, I inclose herewith for
                    communication to the Belgian Government a copy of a note<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d23-f1"/> addressed on April 17, 1900, by the secretary of state of
                    Liberia to the United States charge d’affaires ad interim at Monrovia announcing
                    the adhesion of Liberia to the convention of June 8, 1899, governing the sale of
                    spirituous liquors in certain portions of Africa.</p>
                <p>Mr. Spurgeon has been instructed to inform the Liberian Government that the
                    notification of this adhesion should also be sent directly to the Belgian
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d23-f1" n="1" xml:id="d23-f1-content">
                <p>Printed under Liberia.</p>
